--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modified files
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Every file below carries a "Modified from ..." header naming its upstream and
its changes. Modifications are Copyright 2026 Dongyoon Kim, released under the
Apache License, Version 2.0.

patched/train.py
  Upstream: vlash/train.py (vlash, commit 22cbabf)
  - Added module-level _resize_with_pad / _resize_with_pad_then_aug, which
    letterbox every camera frame to 224x224. Injected as image_transforms only
    when the dataset carries "<camera>_mask" columns, so mixed-resolution
    sources can be collated without re-encoding any video.
  - Checkpointing on the LoRA branch: save adapters only, skipping the merged
    model weights and the training state, and export the normalization buffers
    to normalize_buffers.pt.
  - Added S3 resume/archive uploads and a local rolling prune, driven by the
    SLOT_ID, S3_CKPT_BASE and RESUME_FREQ environment variables. Inactive when
    those variables are unset.
  - Pin the W&B run id and job name to the slot id and force resume="allow"
    when an S3 slot is configured, so a restarted preemptible instance appends
    to the same run.

patched/modeling_pi05.py
  Upstream: vlash/policies/pi05/modeling_pi05.py (vlash, commit 22cbabf)
  - Drop "<camera>_mask" columns from config.input_features so normalization
    cannot alter the 0/1 flags.
  - prepare_images reads "<camera>_mask" per sample and uses it as the image
    attention mask, instead of marking every image valid.
  - Load the PaliGemma tokenizer from a local directory when
    VLASH_PALIGEMMA_PATH is set, instead of always going through the Hugging
    Face hub or cache. The default remains the upstream Hub id, so the change
    is a no-op unless the variable is set; the training image sets it.

patched/run.py
  Upstream: vlash/run.py (vlash, commit 22cbabf)
  - Blend action chunk boundaries with a linear ramp over the overlap window.
  - validate_robot_cameras accepts a robot camera set that is a subset of the
    policy's image features instead of requiring an exact match, so a two-camera
    robot can run a three-slot policy. A camera the policy does not know still
    raises ValueError.
  - run_loop honours VLASH_DRY_RUN=1 (predict without sending actions) and
    aborts when a joint exceeds VLASH_SAFE_DEG degrees.
  - load_and_compile_policy loads adapter-only checkpoints (base weights plus a
    LoRA merge) and restores dataset statistics from normalize_buffers.pt.

patched/video_utils.py
  Upstream: lerobot/datasets/video_utils.py (LeRobot 0.4.1)
  - VideoDecoderCache is bounded by an LRU of VLASH_DECODER_CACHE_MAX entries
    (default 64) and closes the file handle on eviction. The upstream cache is
    unbounded and grows without limit over a long run across many videos
    (upstream issues #2371, #3712).
  - decode_video_frames_torchcodec logs the offending video path and falls back
    to frame 0 on a decoder error, instead of aborting the training run.

